`env/env_0046_home_improvement_retailer` is finished and passes all three delivery conditions. All 5 difficulties pass the policy audit and all 5 published knowledge bases pass their audit. The final `validate_scenario` run on the whole scenario prints `VALID`.

The scenario is Ridgeline Home Center, a 612-store home improvement chain. It has 7 products, and 5 of them each belong to one difficulty with 2 tasks:

| Difficulty | Product | Policy audit | KB audit |
|---|---|---|---|
| `consumer_credit_servicing` | card (55 docs) | PASS, round 2 | PASS, round 1 |
| `pro_credit_account_servicing` | trade (72 docs) | PASS, round 2 | PASS, round 1 |
| `installation_contract_servicing` | install (68 docs) | PASS, round 1 | PASS, round 3 |
| `tool_rental_servicing` | rental (74 docs) | PASS, round 4 | PASS, round 2 |
| `special_order_servicing` | special (63 docs) | PASS, round 2 | PASS, round 2 |

I re-ran every gate myself at the end and all are green, including the traceability check that needs the published docs.

**Cross-difficulty check:** before the docs were rendered, I checked that no phone number, email, name or tax ID repeats across difficulties; none does. The blueprint gates still pass.

Things you should know:
- **Two products were never audited.** `pro` (ProBuild Rewards loyalty, 23 docs) and `order` (online orders and delivery, 19 docs) belong to no difficulty. Only their own render checks stand behind them; no audit ever compared them against their source.
- **One gap is accepted as a known issue.** The special-order delay-credit policy retires the old amount rule for every program, but its replacement only covers deposit programs. Cut-to-Order Flooring and Made-to-Measure Window Coverings therefore have no delay-credit amount anywhere in the KB. Both auditors confirmed no task depends on it, so I logged it rather than sending it back.
- **Some smaller source gaps remain.** The installation charter has wording mismatches between rules and formulas (labelled K0-2, K0-3, (a) and (b)); the auditor confirmed none changes a scored value. Every audit report also lists observations that didn't count as failures.
- **Re-audits weren't blind.** From round 2 onward, auditors had already seen the answer keys, and each report says so. The round-1 blind answers remain the blind evidence.

The worklog at `env/env_0046_home_improvement_retailer/worklog.md` records every launch, resume and verdict, and ends with a DELIVERED line. The run was cut by account limits several times; each time I checked what was on disk and resumed the same agent rather than starting a new one. The empty `.doc_render_staging/` folder is left in place because the render instructions say not to delete it. Nothing was committed.
